# Vell the elder (US-270): the written dialogue of the test level. What she says depends on what she thinks of you (opinion of -100 to 100).
@who npc-vell

=== start
Vell: The fire keeps you well, {hero}.   [if opinion(npc, hero) >= 10]
Vell: Sit. Ask what you will.   [if opinion(npc, hero) >= 10]
Vell: I know your face, {hero}. Not yet your heart.   [if opinion(npc, hero) < 10]
-> Ask about the clan => clan
-> Ask about the stones => stones
-> Speak kindly {opinion npc hero 5; remember npc "{hero} spoke kindly at the fire" 20} => kind
-> Leave => END

=== clan
Vell: A clan is people who share a fire, nothing more.
-> Back => start

=== stones
Vell: The stones are older than the clan. Leave the goblin to them.
-> Back => start

=== kind
Vell: Words cost nothing. That is why I weigh them.
-> Back => start
